# The api and web images build from the repo root, so npm ci can use package-lock.json. Send only what
# their Dockerfiles copy: no local installs or build output, and never a .env (on a server it holds the
# production secrets). services/ai builds from its own folder and has its own .dockerignore.
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!e2e/package.json
!apps/api
!apps/web
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.env*
# Written by the api build (scripts/copy-fonts.mjs).
apps/api/fonts
# The static interactive preview (recorded fixtures and export) is not part of the server image.
apps/web/preview-data
apps/web/out
